      "search_text": "Advanced Game Design: A Systems Approach MDA: A Formal Approach to Game Design and Game Research mid-level systems reasoning vs compact formal framing Use MDA as the compact alignment frame, then use A Systems Approach to reason through how the interacting loops actually create or break that alignment. You need a concise way to align mechanics, dynamics, and aesthetics across the team. You need to unpack how multiple loops and dependencies interact after that top-line alignment is clear. Start with MDA for the frame and escalate to A Systems Approach when the system still feels tangled. 中层系统梳理 循环关系审查 体系化设计复盘"
